From ecddd08e7425e72b2abf53a532bb0c84b6a9ba36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 06:20:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ICMR: per-patient/multi/all CSV, Top 5 in CSV, hospital Study
 ID, reorder fields

Task 1 (dashboard.py): View Records grid is now multi-row selectable.
- 'Download All' exports every patient in the current filter (Select All).
- Selecting multiple rows shows 'Download Selected (N)'.
- A single selection keeps the View/Edit/Update DR/Delete action bar and adds
  a per-patient 'CSV' download.

Task 2 (dashboard.py): downloaded CSV now includes the Top 5 predicted viruses
with probabilities (Top 1..5 Virus + Probability % columns), one row per
patient. The values are already stored on each record, so nothing is recomputed
and the model is never touched.

Task 3 (data_handler.py + app.py): Patient Study ID is auto-generated per
hospital (MMC -> M01, TMC -> T01, ...) via a per-hospital atomic MongoDB
counter, assigned at enrolment. Existing records are untouched. app.py shows the
assigned Study ID after enrolment and a read-only placeholder on the form.

Task 4 (app.py): prediction inputs reordered to Date of Collection, Patient MRD
ID, Hospital, Patient Study ID (auto), Department, Date of Admission, Patient
Name, Address, Mobile No.

No model/.pth files touched. No prediction logic changed.

